Here's the modified code for the ban command that allows you to provide a custom message as an argument:


```javascript
const { Client, Intents } = require('discord.js');

const client = new Client({
  intents: [Intents.FLAGS.GUILDS]
});

client.on('ready', () => {
  console.log(`Logged in as ${client.user.tag}!`);
});

client.on('interactionCreate', async interaction => {
  if (!interaction.isCommand()) return;

  if (interaction.commandName === 'ban') {
    // Get the user to be banned
    const user = interaction.options.getUser('user');

    // Get the reason for the ban from the user-provided argument
    const reason = interaction.options.getString('reason') || 'No reason provided';

    // Ban the user
    await interaction.guild.members.ban(user, { reason });

    // Respond with the ban message
    await interaction.reply(`${user.username} has been banned. Reason: ${reason}`);
  }
});

client.login('your-token-here');
```

With this code, you can use the `/ban` command with a `user` option and an optional `reason` option. The `reason` option allows you to specify a custom message for the ban. If the `reason` option is not provided, the default message "No reason provided" will be used.
